<reference xml:id="class.io-poll-watcher" role="class" xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
 <title>The Io\Poll\Watcher class</title>
 <titleabbrev>Io\Poll\Watcher</titleabbrev>

 <partintro>
  <section xml:id="io-poll-watcher.intro">
   &reftitle.intro;
   <simpara>
    A watcher represents the registration of an
    <classname>Io\Poll\Handle</classname> with an
    <classname>Io\Poll\Context</classname>.
    It is returned by <methodname>Io\Poll\Context::add</methodname>, and by
    <methodname>Io\Poll\Context::wait</methodname> when one of its events was
    triggered.
   </simpara>
   <simpara>
    The watcher gives access to the handle, to the events it is registered
    for, to the events that were last reported, and to an arbitrary value that
    the application associated with it.
    It is also used to change the registration or to end it.
   </simpara>
   <simpara>
    Objects of this class cannot be instantiated directly, cloned or
    serialized.
   </simpara>
  </section>

